# REST API for Book Management — Complete Implementation

## Overview

This project implements a fully functional REST API using **Node.js** and **Express.js** that manages a collection of books with full CRUD operations (Create, Read, Update, Delete) plus statistics. The entire application is organized into multiple files following the **separation of concerns** principle: routing logic lives in `src/routes/books.js`, error handling is centralized in `src/errors/` and `src/middleware/errorHandler.js`, and the Express server bootstrap is in `server.js`. We use an **in-memory array** as our data store (no database required), which keeps the example self-contained and easy to run. Every function includes comprehensive JSDoc documentation, every endpoint has detailed comments explaining REST conventions, and thorough error handling is provided via custom error classes and middleware. The API supports filtering on `GET /books` by author, genre, and year range, and returns statistics on `GET /stats`.

