## Design Decisions

### In-Memory Storage
We use an in-memory array instead of a database to keep the project simple and focused on API patterns. For production, replace `src/models/books.js` with a database adapter.

### Error Handling Pattern
Custom error classes extend a base `AppError` that carries HTTP status codes. The centralized error-handling middleware catches all errors and returns consistent JSON responses.

### REST Conventions
- GET requests are safe and idempotent
- POST creates new resources (returns 201)
- PUT performs full updates (idempotent)
- DELETE removes resources (idempotent)
- All responses use a success/data envelope

