# 📚 Book REST API

A complete CRUD REST API for managing books, built with Node.js and Express.js.
Designed as an educational example with detailed comments throughout.

## Prerequisites

- [Node.js](https://nodejs.org/) v18 or higher
- npm (comes with Node.js)

## Installation

```bash
# Clone or navigate to the project directory
npm install
```

## Running the API

### Development mode (auto-restart on file changes):
```bash
npm run dev
```

### Production mode:
```bash
npm start
```

The server starts at `http://localhost:3000` by default.
Override the port with: `PORT=8080 npm start`

## API Endpoints

| Method | Endpoint          | Description                  |
|--------|-------------------|------------------------------|
| GET    | /books            | List all books (with filters)|
| GET    | /books/:id        | Get a single book            |
| POST   | /books            | Create a new book            |
| PUT    | /books/:id        | Update an existing book      |
| DELETE | /books/:id        | Delete a book                |
| GET    | /stats            | Collection statistics        |

## Testing with curl

### List all books
```bash
curl http://localhost:3000/books
```

### List books filtered by genre
```bash
curl "http://localhost:3000/books?genre=Fiction"
```

### Search books (title or author)
```bash
curl "http://localhost:3000/books?search=gatsby"
```

### Get a single book
```bash
curl http://localhost:3000/books/1
```

### Create a new book
```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/books \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"title":"Brave New World","author":"Aldous Huxley","genre":"Dystopian","year":1932}'
```

### Update a book (PUT — full update)
```bash
curl -X PUT http://localhost:3000/books/1 \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"title":"To Kill a Mockingbird (Annotated Edition)","year":1960}'
```

### Delete a book
```bash
curl -X DELETE http://localhost:3000/books/1
```

### Get statistics
```bash
curl http://localhost:3000/stats
```

## Project Structure

```
src/
├── app.js              # Entry point — wires everything together
├── models/
│   └── book.js         # Book data shape and factory functions
├── data/
│   └── booksData.js    # In-memory storage layer (CRUD operations)
├── services/
│   └── bookService.js  # Business logic and validation
├── middleware/
│   └── errorHandler.js # Custom errors + Express error handler
└── routes/
    ├── books.js        # Book CRUD endpoints
    └── stats.js        # Statistics endpoint
```

## Architecture Layers

```
Client Request
      │
      ▼
  Routes (books.js, stats.js)     ← Parse input, send output
      │
      ▼
  Service (bookService.js)         ← Validation, business rules
      │
      ▼
  Data (booksData.js)              ← Storage operations
      │
      ▼
  Model (book.js)                  ← Object shape & factories
```

## Error Response Format

All errors follow this consistent JSON structure:

```json
{
  "error": "Book with id 99 not found",
  "statusCode": 404,
  "type": "NotFoundError"
}
```

### Error Types

| Type              | Status | When                                      |
|-------------------|--------|-------------------------------------------|
| ValidationError   | 400    | Missing/invalid request data              |
| NotFoundError     | 404    | Resource doesn't exist                    |
| ConflictError     | 409    | Duplicate title                           |
| Error             | 500    | Unexpected server error                   |
```

